        </div>

        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:14px;margin-top:26px">
          <div class="prow" style="border:0;padding:0"><span class="prow__k">Market cap</span><span class="prow__v">$1.18M</span></div>
          <div class="prow" style="border:0;padding:0"><span class="prow__k">Total burned</span><span class="prow__v">4.82M $ONLY</span></div>
        </div>

        <div style="display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:28px">
          <a class="btn btn--primary" href="https://pump.fun/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Buy on pump.fun ↗</a>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="#how">How the buyback works</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="sidecard rv">
        <div class="eyebrow">Why it burns — and why it pays</div>
        <p class="muted" style="font-size:.94rem;margin-top:14px">
          The OnlyVault is the product. The buyback is the pressure valve. Every Only launched here pushes 5% of
          its reward into buying <b>$ONLY</b> off the market. <b>Half is destroyed</b>, so supply only moves one
          direction. The <b>other half is paid back to the Subs</b>, in 15-minute Drops.
        </p>
        <div class="hairline" style="margin:24px 0"></div>
        <div class="prow"><span class="prow__k">Pad treasury</span><span class="prow__v">pad…only</span></div>
        <div class="prow"><span class="prow__k">Burn share</span><span class="prow__v primary">50%</span></div>
        <div class="prow"><span class="prow__k">Tip Jar share</span><span class="prow__v secondary">50%</span></div>
        <div class="prow"><span class="prow__k">Drop length</span><span class="prow__v">15 min</span></div>
        <div class="prow"><span class="prow__k">Burn address</span><span class="prow__v">1nc1nerator…</span></div>
        <div style="margin-top:auto;padding-top:26px">
          <a class="btnlink" href="#jar">See the current jar →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================= HOW ================= -->
<section class="sec" id="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head rv">
      <div class="eyebrow">How it works</div>
      <h2 class="h-xl">Launch → vault → sub → claim.</h2>
      <p class="lead">One vault per Only, for life. The split is written on chain by pump.fun at launch, so nobody can change it later — not us, and not the launcher.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="how">
      <div class="howcard rv">
        <div class="howcard__n">01</div>
        <div class="howcard__t">Launch an Only for a creator</div>
        <p class="howcard__d">Pick <b>Creator Launch</b> or <b>Fan Launch</b>, choose how Subs claim, set the creator's Cut, add an image and a name, and launch on pump.fun from your own wallet. The OnlyVault and the escrow account are created with it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="howcard rv">
        <div class="howcard__n">02</div>
        <div class="howcard__t">Every trade pays the creator</div>
        <p class="howcard__d">Each trade of the coin earns a creator reward. <b>The Cut goes to the creator's wallet</b> — or to Creator Escrow if they have not verified yet. <b>35%</b> flows into the OnlyVault and starts accruing to Subs. <b>5%</b> buys and burns $ONLY.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="howcard rv">
        <div class="howcard__n">03</div>
        <div class="howcard__t">Sub, hold, claim anytime</div>
        <p class="howcard__d">A Sub's share is their balance multiplied by their sub streak. Claim whenever you like — <b>the vault keeps filling</b>, and the Subs who never sold keep taking the biggest cut of it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flow" style="margin-top:22px">
      <div class="flow__resolver rv" style="grid-column:1/-1">
        <div class="ic">
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 2v20M17 5H9.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 0 0 7h5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 0 7H6"/></svg>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="h-md">Where the reward goes</div>
          <p class="muted" style="font-size:.93rem;margin-top:7px">
            Every Only has its pump.fun creator reward split on chain at launch: <b>the creator's Cut</b>, which is
            theirs and is paid on every trade; <b>35% to the OnlyVault</b>, which accrues to Subs and is claimed by
            them; and <b>5% to the Pad</b>, which buys $ONLY on the open market and burns half of it. pump.fun only
            lets the split be set once, so nobody can change it later.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================= TIERS ================= -->
<section class="sec" id="tiers">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head rv">
      <div class="eyebrow">Proof of Sub</div>
      <h2 class="h-xl">The longer you stay subscribed, the bigger your Tips.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Your weight is your balance multiplied by your sub streak. The ladder is counted in <b>renewals</b> — thirty-day periods, the way a subscription is counted anywhere else.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tiers rv">
      <div class="tier">
        <div class="tier__day">Day 1</div>
        <div class="tier__name">Fresh <small>just found them</small></div>
        <div class="tier__mult">1.0×</div>
        <div class="tier__bar"><i style="width:20%"></i></div>
      </div>
      <div class="tier">
        <div class="tier__day">1 renewal</div>
        <div class="tier__name">Subscribed <small>first month paid</small></div>
        <div class="tier__mult">1.5×</div>
        <div class="tier__bar"><i style="width:37%"></i></div>
      </div>
      <div class="tier">
        <div class="tier__day">3 renewals</div>
        <div class="tier__name">Renewed <small>stuck around</small></div>
        <div class="tier__mult">2.5×</div>
        <div class="tier__bar"><i style="width:62%"></i></div>
      </div>
      <div class="tier">
        <div class="tier__day">6 renewals</div>
        <div class="tier__name">Loyal <small>half a year unbroken</small></div>
        <div class="tier__mult">4.0×</div>
        <div class="tier__bar"><i style="width:82%"></i></div>
      </div>
      <div class="tier tier--top">
        <div class="tier__day">12 renewals</div>
        <div class="tier__name">Founding Sub <small>a year, never sold</small></div>
        <div class="tier__mult">5.0×</div>
        <div class="tier__bar"><i style="width:100%"></i></div>
      </div>
      <div class="tier" style="display:block;padding:20px 24px">
        <p class="muted" style="font-size:.9rem">
          <b style="color:var(--danger)">Selling resets you to 1.0×.</b> Any sell — even a partial one — resets your
          sub streak, and Tips you had accrued but not yet claimed return to the OnlyVault for the Subs who stayed.
          Claiming does not reset anything. Only selling does. And none of it touches the creator's Cut.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================= FAQ ================= -->
<section class="sec" id="faq">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head rv">
      <div class="eyebrow">FAQ</div>
      <h2 class="h-xl">Questions.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="faq rv" id="faqList">

      <div class="fitem">
        <button class="fq" type="button">
          <span class="fq__t">Does this connect to OnlyFans?</span>
          <span class="fq__ic"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span>
        </button>
        <div class="fa"><div class="fa__in">
          <b>No, and it cannot.</b> OnlyFans has no public API and no deposit address, so nothing outside it can credit an account there — every "OnlyFans API" you can find is an unofficial reseller that logs in as the creator, which is a ban risk. So the Cut is paid in <b>SOL to a wallet</b> the creator controls. It is instant, it needs nobody's permission, and it keeps working even if they leave the platform. OnlyPad is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to OnlyFans.
        </div></div>
      </div>

      <div class="fitem">
        <button class="fq" type="button">
          <span class="fq__t">Do I get my coin's creator reward?</span>
          <span class="fq__ic"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span>
        </button>
        <div class="fa"><div class="fa__in">
          Not unless you are the creator. On a <b>Creator Launch</b> the Cut is yours because the coin is for you. On a <b>Fan Launch</b> it belongs to the creator and sits in escrow until they claim it — the fan who launched it gets no share of it, ever. That is deliberate: the whole point is that the money goes to the person the coin is named after.
        </div></div>
      </div>

      <div class="fitem">
        <button class="fq" type="button">
          <span class="fq__t">What exactly do Subs claim?</span>
          <span class="fq__ic"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span>
        </button>
        <div class="fa"><div class="fa__in">
          The coin's <b>Tips</b> — the 35% of the pump.fun creator reward that flows into that coin's OnlyVault. There is no separate token to farm and no lockup on claiming: the vault fills as the coin trades, and every Sub has a standing claim on it weighted by their balance and their sub streak.
        </div></div>
      </div>

      <div class="fitem">
        <button class="fq" type="button">
          <span class="fq__t">What is the difference between a Creator Launch and a Fan Launch?</span>
          <span class="fq__ic"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span>
        </button>
        <div class="fa"><div class="fa__in">
          On a <b>Creator Launch</b> the creator launches it themselves and signs a challenge proving the handle is theirs. The coin carries a <b>VERIFIED</b> badge and the Cut streams to their wallet from the first trade. On a <b>Fan Launch</b> anyone can start a coin for a creator who has not opted in. It carries an <b>UNCLAIMED</b> badge, cannot use the creator's name or likeness, and the Cut accrues in Creator Escrow until they verify. Nothing is withheld from them — it is waiting.
        </div></div>
      </div>

      <div class="fitem">
        <button class="fq" type="button">
          <span class="fq__t">What happens if I sell?</span>
          <span class="fq__ic"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span>
        </button>
        <div class="fa"><div class="fa__in">
          Your sub streak resets to zero, so your multiplier drops back to 1.0×, and <b>Tips you had accrued but not yet claimed go back into the OnlyVault</b> for the Subs who stayed. Anything you already claimed is yours and is not clawed back. Claiming changes nothing about your weight — you can claim as often as you like. Selling never affects the creator's Cut.
        </div></div>
      </div>

      <div class="fitem">
        <button class="fq" type="button">
          <span class="fq__t">Can the split change later?</span>
          <span class="fq__ic"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span>
        </button>
        <div class="fa"><div class="fa__in">
          No. pump.fun only lets a coin's fee-sharing configuration be set once, at launch. The creator's Cut, the OnlyVault address, the escrow address and the Pad treasury are fixed the moment the coin is created — not by us, and not by the launcher.
        </div></div>
      </div>

      <div class="fitem">
        <button class="fq" type="button">
          <span class="fq__t">Who can have a coin on the Pad?</span>
          <span class="fq__ic"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span>
        </button>
        <div class="fa"><div class="fa__in">
          <b>Verified adults only, and the Pad is 18+.</b> There is no adult content anywhere on this site — no images from any platform, nothing explicit. A coin can only be created for a creator who has verified as an adult, and any coin created for or by a minor is removed and burned immediately. That rule is not negotiable and will not be softened.
        </div></div>
      </div>

      <div class="fitem">
        <button class="fq" type="button">
          <span class="fq__t">Is it free to launch?</span>
          <span class="fq__ic"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg></span>
        </button>
        <div class="fa"><div class="fa__in">
          Yes. OnlyPad does not charge anything, and pump.fun does not charge to create a coin. The only cost is Solana's own network cost, about <code>0.01 SOL</code>, which is mostly a one-time deposit for the coin's new accounts on chain. It comes from your wallet, and your wallet shows it before you sign. A dev buy is optional and extra.
        </div></div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ================= BAND ================= -->
